    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/ysu/Faculty/jobs/5480161/lecturer-physics-physics-astronomy-term": {
      "title": "Lecturer, Physics – Physics & Astronomy (Term)",
      "description": "Lecturer, Physics – Physics & Astronomy (Term) Location Youngstown, Ohio Job Type Full-time Faculty Job Number 202600257 Division Academic Affairs Department Physics & Astronomy Opening Date 09/11/2026 Bargaining Unit Status Ohio Education Association (OEA) Salary Grade LECT Description Benefits Questions Summary of Position Teach physics courses and associated laboratory courses at the baccalaureate level. Courses may include general education science courses, introductory courses for physics majors, and upper-division physics courses. Responsibilities include preparing and delivering lectures; organizing and supervising laboratory sections; developing in-class learning activities; writing and grading examinations and laboratory reports; and holding office hours to address student questions and provide additional academic support. Maintain an inventory of laboratory supplies and equipment needed for laboratory and lecture courses and submit order requests to departmental administrative support in a timely manner. Additional responsibilities include participating in course and program assessment, curriculum development and improvement, and other education-related activities. Encouraged to incorporate innovative instructional methods and educational enrichment activities, including demonstrations, supplemental videos, and student projects. This appointment focused primarily on teaching and does not include scholarly activity expectations. Teaching responsibilities appropriate to the term appointment, with minimal service expectations. Service may include participation in department, college, and university activities; student advising; and community outreach. Position Information Plans, organizes, teaches, and provides feedback to promote and direct student success. Responds to students in a timely manner. Communicates with students, departments, and university officials via university provided tools and resources. An Institution of Opportunity: YSU inspires individuals, enhances futures, and enriches lives. As a student-centered university, Youngstown State University’s mission is to provide innovative lifelong learning opportunities that will inspire individuals, enhance futures and enrich lives. YSU inspires individuals by cultivating a curiosity for life-long learning; enhances the futures of our students by empowering them to discover, disseminate and apply their knowledge; and enriches the region by fostering collaboration and the advancement of civic, scientific, and technological development. YSU’s culture of enrichment flourishes in our intellectually diverse, accessible, and quality education. Work Schedule: Typically, Monday through Friday, including some evenings, and the possibility of some weekend days. Primary Location: Youngstown Qualifications and Competencies Required Certifications, Training, and/or Licensures: None. Sponsorship and/or Work Authorization Status: This position is not eligible for sponsorship. Minimum Qualifications: At least an earned Master of Science degree or higher in physics; teaching experience in physics coursework at the college level. Preferred Qualifications: Extensive teaching experience at the college level in physics. Physical Requirements: In accordance with the U.S. Department of Labor physical demands strength ratings, this position will perform sedentary work. Sedentary: work involves exerting up to 10 pounds of force occasionally or a negligible amount of force frequently to lift, carry, push, pull, or otherwise move objects, including the human body. Sedentary work involves sitting most of the time but may involve walking or standing for brief periods of time. Jobs may be defined as Sedentary when walking and standing are required only occasionally, and all other Sedentary criteria are met. Supplemental Information Please upload all transcripts as one PDF file. At time of hire, all candidates must provide official transcripts. Official transcripts must be provided in an unopened, sealed envelope and must bear the embossed or raised college seal, date and Registrar’s signature. Position expected start date: Spring 2027 At Youngstown State University we are committed to a comprehensive employee benefit program that helps our employees live healthy, feel secure, and maintain a work/life balance. YSU offers two options for medical plans, optional dental and vision insurance and life insurance. These plans are reviewed annually to maintain competitiveness while being cost effective. In addition, YSU offers tuition remission, 403(b) and 457 retirement planning options, as well as state pension programs and optional voluntary life insurance benefits. Medical Mutual of Ohio Medical plans Dental Benefits Vision Benefits Group Life Insurance (University Sponsored and Voluntary) Group Long Term Disability (University Sponsored and Voluntary) Flexible Spending Account Health Savings Account Tuition remission Employee Assistance Program Wellness Initiatives Sick Leave Vacation Accrual Paid Holidays State Retirement Programs 403b and 457b Voluntary Retirement Options 01 Do you have at least an earned Master of Science degree or higher in physics? Yes No 02 Do you have teaching experience in physics coursework at the college level? Yes No 03 What is the highest level of education that you have attained? Did not complete high school. High school diploma/GED or equivalent Some college Associate's degree Bachelor's degree Master's degree Doctoral degree Post doctoral degree Juris doctor degree 04 Please describe your related experience, including information describing how you meet the minimum qualifications for this position. Required Question Employer Youngstown State University (OH) Address 1 Tressel Way Youngstown, Ohio, 44555 Phone 330-941-1508 Website http://www.ysu.edu Apply"
    },
    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/ysu/Faculty/jobs/5480041/lecturer-psych-np-nursing-term": {
      "title": "Lecturer, Psych NP – Nursing (Term)",
      "description": "Lecturer, Psych NP – Nursing (Term) Location Youngstown, Ohio Job Type Full-time Faculty Job Number 202600253 Division Academic Affairs Department Nursing Opening Date 09/11/2026 Bargaining Unit Status Ohio Education Association (OEA) Salary Grade LECT Description Benefits Questions Summary of Position Provide instruction to graduate nursing students, with a primary focus on advanced practice. Responsibilities include teaching and facilitating student learning through evidence-based instructional strategies; and managing student coursework and communication through online learning platforms. In addition to teaching, the position includes participation as the Psych NP program director, development of the program, and service activities that support the mission of the department, college, and university, such as mentoring students, contributing to curriculum development, and engaging with the professional community. Position Information Plans, organizes, teaches, and provides feedback to promote and direct student success. Responds to students in a timely manner. Communicates with students, departments, and university officials via university provided tools and resources. An Institution of Opportunity: YSU inspires individuals, enhances futures, and enriches lives. As a student-centered university, Youngstown State University’s mission is to provide innovative lifelong learning opportunities that will inspire individuals, enhance futures and enrich lives. YSU inspires individuals by cultivating a curiosity for life-long learning; enhances the futures of our students by empowering them to discover, disseminate and apply their knowledge; and enriches the region by fostering collaboration and the advancement of civic, scientific, and technological development. YSU’s culture of enrichment flourishes in our intellectually diverse, accessible, and quality education. Work Schedule: Typically, Monday through Friday, including some evenings, and the possibility of some weekend days. Primary Location: Youngstown Qualifications and Competencies Required Certifications, Training, and/or Licensures: Unencumbered Ohio Registered Nurse license (RN) by the time of appointment. Certification in field of study Psych Nurse Practitioner. Sponsorship and/or Work Authorization Status: This position is not eligible for sponsorship. Minimum Qualifications: An earned master’s and bachelor’s degree of Science in Nursing (MSN and BSN); unencumbered active Ohio Registered Nurse license (RN) at the time of employment; certification in field of study Psych Nurse Practitioner. Preferred Qualifications: Doctor of Nursing Practice (DNP), PhD, or dual certification of Family Nurse Practitioner (FNP) or Adult Gero- Acute Care Nurse Practitioner (AG-ACNP) along with Psych Nurse Practitioner. Physical Requirements: In accordance with the U.S. Department of Labor physical demands strength ratings, this position will perform sedentary work. Sedentary: work involves exerting up to 10 pounds of force occasionally or a negligible amount of force frequently to lift, carry, push, pull, or otherwise move objects, including the human body. Sedentary work involves sitting most of the time but may involve walking or standing for brief periods of time. Jobs may be defined as Sedentary when walking and standing are required only occasionally, and all other Sedentary criteria are met. Supplemental Information Please upload all transcripts as one PDF file. At time of hire, all candidates must provide official transcripts. Official transcripts must be provided in an unopened, sealed envelope and must bear the embossed or raised college seal, date and Registrar’s signature. At Youngstown State University we are committed to a comprehensive employee benefit program that helps our employees live healthy, feel secure, and maintain a work/life balance. YSU offers two options for medical plans, optional dental and vision insurance and life insurance. These plans are reviewed annually to maintain competitiveness while being cost effective. In addition, YSU offers tuition remission, 403(b) and 457 retirement planning options, as well as state pension programs and optional voluntary life insurance benefits. Medical Mutual of Ohio Medical plans Dental Benefits Vision Benefits Group Life Insurance (University Sponsored and Voluntary) Group Long Term Disability (University Sponsored and Voluntary) Flexible Spending Account Health Savings Account Tuition remission Employee Assistance Program Wellness Initiatives Sick Leave Vacation Accrual Paid Holidays State Retirement Programs 403b and 457b Voluntary Retirement Options 01 Do you have at least an earned master’s and bachelor’s degree of Science in Nursing (MSN and BSN)? Yes No 02 Do you or will you have an unencumbered active Ohio Registered Nurse license (RN) at the time of employment? Yes No 03 Do you have certification in the field of study Psych Nurse Practitioner? Yes No 04 What is the highest level of education that you have attained? Did not complete high school. High school diploma/GED or equivalent Some college Associate's degree Bachelor's degree Master's degree Doctoral degree Post doctoral degree Juris doctor degree 05 Please describe your related experience, including information describing how you meet the minimum qualifications for this position. Required Question Employer Youngstown State University (OH) Address 1 Tressel Way Youngstown, Ohio, 44555 Phone 330-941-1508 Website http://www.ysu.edu Apply"
