nrichment flourishes in our intellectually diverse, accessible, and quality education. Work Schedule: Typically, Monday through Friday. Able to travel to any of the districts in the following counties: Mahoning, Trumbull, Columbiana, Mercer, and Lawrence. Primary Location: Youngstown Qualifications and Competencies Required Certifications, Training, and/or Licensures: Certified/licensed in K-12 teaching field in which supervision occurs; valid driver’s license. Sponsorship and/or Work Authorization Status: Must be currently authorized to work in the United States on a full-time basis. Minimum Qualifications: At least a bachelor’s degree in education (K-12 teaching field); ten or more years of teaching experience (K-12 teaching field); three or more years of experience mentoring student teachers or teacher candidates in the field; certified/licensed in K-12 teaching field in which supervision occurs; minimum fifty hours of documented professional development within past ten years; valid driver’s license. Must be currently authorized to work in the United States on a full-time basis. Preferred Qualifications: Trained mentor. Knowledge of the Resident Educator Summative Assessment (RESA) and/or Education Teacher Preparation Assessment (edTPA). Completed OTES training and/or other evaluator training. Recent P-12 teaching and/or administrative experience; knowledge of technology used in teaching. Physical Requirements: In accordance with the U.S. Department of Labor physical demands strength ratings, this position will perform sedentary work. Sedentary: work involves exerting up to 10 pounds of force occasionally or a negligible amount of force frequently to lift, carry, push, pull, or otherwise move objects, including the human body. Sedentary work involves sitting most of the time but may involve walking or standing for brief periods of time. Jobs may be defined as Sedentary when walking and standing are required only occasionally, and all other Sedentary criteria are 