      "title": "Part-time Faculty, Undergraduate Nursing Clinical - Nursing",
      "description": "Part-time Faculty, Undergraduate Nursing Clinical - Nursing Location Multiple Locations Job Type Part-time Faculty Job Number 202600123 Division Academic Affairs Department Nursing Opening Date 04/14/2026 Closing Date 4/14/2027 11:59 PM Eastern Bargaining Unit Status Excluded from Any Bargaining Unit Salary Grade PF Additional Information Part-time faculty are pooled positions; appointments are made on an as-needed/rolling basis. Description Benefits Questions Summary of Position Teach and support undergraduate nursing students in both clinical and laboratory settings by supervising hands-on learning experiences and guiding the development of essential nursing skills. Responsibilities include facilitating simulation scenarios that strengthen clinical reasoning and decision making, evaluating student performance, and providing timely, constructive feedback to promote growth. Additional duties involve grading weekly assignments and clinical documentation, ensuring that students effectively integrate classroom theory into practice while maintaining a safe, supportive, and high-quality learning environment. Position Information Plans, organizes, teaches, and provides feedback to promote and direct student success. Responds to students in a timely manner. Communicates with students, departments, and university officials via university provided tools and resources. An Institution of Opportunity: YSU inspires individuals, enhances futures, and enriches lives. As a student-centered university, Youngstown State University’s mission is to provide innovative lifelong learning opportunities that will inspire individuals, enhance futures, and enrich lives. YSU inspires individuals by cultivating a curiosity for life-long learning; enhances the futures of our students by empowering them to discover, disseminate and apply their knowledge; and enriches the region by fostering collaboration and the advancement of civic, scientific, and technological development. YSU’s culture of enrichment flourishes in our intellectually diverse, accessible, and quality education. Work Schedule: Typically, Monday through Friday. Teaching assignments may be remote or at various locations. Primary Location: Youngstown Qualifications and Competencies Required Certifications, Training, and/or Licensures: Unencumbered, active Ohio Registered Nurse license (RN) at the time of employment. Sponsorship and/or Work Authorization Status: Must be currently authorized to work in the United States on a full-time basis. Minimum Qualifications: At least a Bachelor of Science in Nursing (BSN) from an accredited university; unencumbered Ohio Registered Nurse license (RN); and at least two or more years of experience as a practicing registered nurse. Must be currently authorized to work in the United States on a full-time basis. Must be currently authorized to work in the United States on a full-time basis. Preferred Qualifications: A Master of Science in Nursing (MSN). At least one year of experience teaching undergraduate clinicals in fundamentals, medical-surgical, pediatrics, OB, and/ or mental health nursing. Experience in scenario simulation. Physical Requirements: In accordance with the U.S. Department of Labor physical demands strength ratings, this position will perform sedentary work. Sedentary: work involves exerting up to 10 pounds of force occasionally or a negligible amount of force frequently to lift, carry, push, pull, or otherwise move objects, including the human body. Sedentary work involves sitting most of the time but may involve walking or standing for brief periods of time. Jobs may be defined as Sedentary when walking and standing are required only occasionally, and all other Sedentary criteria are met. Supplemental Information Please upload all transcripts as one PDF file. At time of hire, all candidates must provide official transcripts. Official transcripts must be provided in an unopened, sealed envelope and must bear the embossed or raised college seal, date and Registrar’s signature. This position is not eligible for benefits. 01 Do you have at least a Bachelor of Science in Nursing (BSN) from an accredited university? Yes No 02 Do you have an unencumbered Ohio Registered Nurse license (RN)? Yes No 03 Do you have at least two or more years of experience as a practicing registered nurse? Yes No 04 What is the highest level of education that you have attained? Did not complete high school. High school diploma/GED or equivalent Some college Associate's degree Bachelor's degree Master's degree Doctoral degree Post doctoral degree Juris doctor degree 05 Please describe your related experience, including information describing how you meet the minimum qualifications for this position. Required Question Employer Youngstown State University (OH) Address 1 Tressel Way Youngstown, Ohio, 44555 Phone 330-941-1508 Website http://www.ysu.edu Apply"
    },
    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/ysu/jobs/5303821/part-time-faculty-welding-school-comp-sci-info-engr-tech-steubenville": {
      "title": "Part-time Faculty, Welding - School Comp Sci, Info & Engr Tech - Steubenville",
      "description": "Part-time Faculty, Welding - School Comp Sci, Info & Engr Tech - Steubenville Location Steubenville, Ohio Job Type Part-time Faculty Job Number 202600114 Division Academic Affairs Department School of Technology Opening Date 04/10/2026 Closing Date 4/10/2027 11:59 PM Eastern Bargaining Unit Status Excluded from Any Bargaining Unit Salary Grade PF Additional Information Part-time faculty are pooled positions; appointments are made on an as-needed/rolling basis. Description Benefits Questions Summary of Position Teaches certificate and associate degree courses in welding. Possesses comprehensive experience in Shielded Metal Arc Welding (SMAW), Gas Metal Arc Welding (GMAW/MIG), Flux Cored Arc Welding (FCAW), and Gas Tungsten Arc Welding (GTAW/TIG). Demonstrates a strong commitment to OSHA-compliant safety practices and excels in blueprint creation and interpretation. Brings foundational knowledge in robotic welding systems and numerically controlled cutting, supporting efficient, precise, and high-quality fabrication processes. Must be able to provide regular in-person instruction as assigned. Position Information Plans, organizes, teaches, and provides feedback to promote and direct student success. Responds to students in a timely manner. Communicates with students, departments, and university officials via university provided tools and resources. An Institution of Opportunity: YSU inspires individuals, enhances futures, and enriches lives. As a student-centered university, Youngstown State University’s mission is to provide innovative lifelong learning opportunities that will inspire individuals, enhance futures, and enrich lives. YSU inspires individuals by cultivating a curiosity for life-long learning; enhances the futures of our students by empowering them to discover, disseminate and apply their knowledge; and enriches the region by fostering collaboration and the advancement of civic, scientific, and technological development. YSU’s culture of enrichment flourishes in our intellectually diverse, accessible, and quality education. Work Schedule: Typically, Monday through Friday. Primary Location: Steubenville Qualifications and Competencies Required Certifications, Training, and/or Licensures: AWS or equivalent related certification in one or more welding processes. Sponsorship and/or Work Authorization Status: Must be currently authorized to work in the United States on a full-time basis. Minimum Qualifications: AWS or equivalent related certification in one or more welding processes with a high school diploma or GED; at least three years of practical welding experience in at least one of the following categories: Shielded Metal Arc Welding (SMAW), Gas Metal Arc Welding (GMAW/Mig), Flux Cored Arc Welding (FCAW), Gas Tungsten Arc Welding (GTAW/Tig), OSHA Safety, Blueprint creation and reading, Basic robotic welding, and/or Basic numerically controlled cutting. Must be currently authorized to work in the United States on a full-time basis. Preferred Qualifications: Associate or bachelor’s degree in welding. Experience with basic robotic welding and automated 2D cutting. Certified Welding Educator (CWE) credentials. Certified Welding Inspector (CWI) credentials. NC3 Train-the-Trainer certification. Physical Requirements: In accordance with the U.S. Department of Labor physical demands strength ratings, this position will perform sedentary work. Sedentary: work involves exerting up to 10 pounds of force occasionally or a negligible amount of force frequently to lift, carry, push, pull, or otherwise move objects, including the human body. Sedentary work involves sitting most of the time but may involve walking or standing for brief periods of time. Jobs may be defined as Sedentary when walking and standing are required only occasionally, and all other Sedentary criteria are met. Supplemental Information Please upload all transcripts as one PDF file. At time of hire, all candidates must provide official transcripts. Official transcripts must be provided in an unopened, sealed envelope and must bear the embossed or raised college seal, date and Registrar’s signature. This position is not eligible for benefits. 01 Do you have an AWS or equivalent related certification in one or more welding processes with a high school diploma or GED? Yes No 02 Do you have at least three years of practical welding experience in at least one of the following categories: Shielded Metal Arc Welding (SMAW), Gas Metal Arc Welding (GMAW/Mig), Flux Cored Arc Welding (FCAW), Gas Tungsten Arc Welding (GTAW/Tig), OSHA Safety, Blueprint creation and reading, Basic robotic welding, and/or Basic numerically controlled cutting? Yes No 03 What is the highest level of education that you have attained? Did not complete high school. High school diploma/GED or equivalent Some college Associate's degree Bachelor's degree Master's degree Doctoral degree Post doctoral degree Juris doctor degree 04 Please describe your related experience, including information describing how you meet the minimum qualifications for this position. Required Question Employer Youngstown State University (OH) Address 1 Tressel Way Youngstown, Ohio, 44555 Phone 330-941-1508 Website http://www.ysu.edu Apply"
