    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/ysu/Faculty/jobs/5532743/assistant-professor-analytical-or-physical-chemistry-tenure-track": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor, Analytical or Physical Chemistry (Tenure-Track)",
      "description": "Assistant Professor, Analytical or Physical Chemistry (Tenure-Track) Location Youngstown, Ohio Job Type Full-time Faculty Job Number 202600293 Division Academic Affairs Department Chemistry Opening Date 10/28/2026 Bargaining Unit Status Ohio Education Association (OEA) Salary Grade ASST Description Benefits Questions Summary of Position A committed analytical or computational chemist at the tenure-track assistant professor rank with a research specialization to teach graduate and undergraduate chemistry lecture and laboratory courses and develop and sustain an externally funded research program involving undergraduate, MS students, and possibly Materials Ph.D. students. The YSU programs in Chemistry and Biochemistry housed in the Department of Chemical and Biological Sciences is comprised of 10 full-time tenure track faculty, 3 lecturers, over 100 majors in its BS programs and an active MS program with 25 students. The department offers a rich, hands-on ‘learning through research’ experience for its students. As part of the College of STEM, the department also participates in the YSU Ph.D. program in Materials Science & Engineering . Position Information Plans, organizes, teaches, and provides feedback to promote and direct student success. Responds to students in a timely manner. Communicates with students, departments, and university officials via university provided tools and resources. An Institution of Opportunity: YSU inspires individuals, enhances futures, and enriches lives. As a student-centered university, Youngstown State University’s mission is to provide innovative lifelong learning opportunities that will inspire individuals, enhance futures and enrich lives. YSU inspires individuals by cultivating a curiosity for life-long learning; enhances the futures of our students by empowering them to discover, disseminate and apply their knowledge; and enriches the region by fostering collaboration and the advancement of civic, scientific, and technological development. YSU’s culture of enrichment flourishes in our intellectually diverse, accessible, and quality education. Work Schedule: Typically, Monday through Friday, including some evenings, and the possibility of some weekend days. Primary Location: Youngstown Qualifications and Competencies Required Certifications, Training, and/or Licensures: None Sponsorship and/or Work Authorization Status: Must be currently authorized to work in the United States on a full-time basis. Minimum Qualifications: Ph.D. in Chemistry or closely related discipline by the time of appointment. Preferred Qualifications: Post-doctoral and teaching experience. Established track record in conducting research leading to peer review publications. Physical Requirements: In accordance with the U.S. Department of Labor physical demands strength ratings, this position will perform sedentary work. Sedentary: work involves exerting up to 10 pounds of force occasionally or a negligible amount of force frequently to lift, carry, push, pull, or otherwise move objects, including the human body. Sedentary work involves sitting most of the time but may involve walking or standing for brief periods of time. Jobs may be defined as Sedentary when walking and standing are required only occasionally, and all other Sedentary criteria are met. Supplemental Information Supplemental Information: Please upload a teaching statement (max 2 pages). Please upload a proposed research plan (max 5 pages). Please upload all transcripts as one PDF file. At time of hire, all candidates must provide official transcripts. Official transcripts must be provided in an unopened, sealed envelope and must bear the embossed or raised college seal, date and Registrar’s signature. Position expected start date: August 2027 (fall semester) At Youngstown State University we are committed to a comprehensive employee benefit program that helps our employees live healthy, feel secure, and maintain a work/life balance. YSU offers two options for medical plans, optional dental and vision insurance and life insurance. These plans are reviewed annually to maintain competitiveness while being cost effective. In addition, YSU offers tuition remission, 403(b) and 457 retirement planning options, as well as state pension programs and optional voluntary life insurance benefits. Medical Mutual of Ohio Medical plans Dental Benefits Vision Benefits Group Life Insurance (University Sponsored and Voluntary) Group Long Term Disability (University Sponsored and Voluntary) Flexible Spending Account Health Savings Account Tuition remission Employee Assistance Program Wellness Initiatives Sick Leave Vacation Accrual Paid Holidays State Retirement Programs 403b and 457b Voluntary Retirement Options 01 Do you have, or will you have, a Ph.D. in Chemistry or closely related discipline by the time of appointment? Yes No 02 What is the highest level of education that you have attained? Did not complete high school. High school diploma/GED or equivalent Some college Associate's degree Bachelor's degree Master's degree Doctoral degree Post doctoral degree Juris doctor degree 03 Please describe your related experience, including information describing how you meet the minimum qualifications for this position. Required Question Employer Youngstown State University (OH) Address 1 Tressel Way Youngstown, Ohio, 44555 Phone 330-941-1508 Website http://www.ysu.edu Apply"
    },
    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/ysu/jobs/5534477/part-time-faculty-educational-administration-edad-international-education-le": {
      "title": "Part-time Faculty, Educational Administration (EDAD) – International Education Leadership",
      "description": "Part-time Faculty, Educational Administration (EDAD) – International Education Leadership Location Multiple Locations Job Type Part-time Faculty Job Number 202600299 Division Academic Affairs Department Teacher Education Opening Date 10/29/2026 Closing Date 10/29/2027 11:59 PM Eastern Bargaining Unit Status Excluded from Any Bargaining Unit Salary Grade PF Additional Information Part-time faculty are pooled positions; appointments are made on an as-needed/rolling basis. Description Benefits Questions Summary of Position Teach graduate coursework within the EdD in International Education Leadership track. This posting is for three separate part-time adjunct faculty positions with expertise in study abroad administration, safety, and risk management; F-1 and J-1 immigration advising and compliance; or international education operations and leadership. Developing and delivering graduate-level instruction within the assigned area of expertise. Responsibilities may include teaching courses in study abroad administration, international program design and assessment, student health and safety, risk management, crisis preparedness and response, immigration advising, regulatory compliance, SEVIS record management, and international education leadership. Prepare students to apply professional standards and best practices in international education; assess and mitigate program risks; develop health, safety, and emergency response protocols; support international student success; evaluate international partners and service providers; maintain compliance with applicable immigration regulations; and navigate complex operational and leadership challenges within higher education institutions. Instruction should incorporate applied learning experiences, case studies, and practical assignments that connect theory to practice and promote effective decision-making, ethical leadership, regulatory compliance, and strategic management in international education. Position Information Plans, organizes, teaches, and provides feedback to promote and direct student success. to students in a timely manner. Communicates with students, departments, and university officials via university provided tools and resources. An Institution of Opportunity: YSU inspires individuals, enhances futures, and enriches lives. As a student-centered university, Youngstown State University’s mission is to provide innovative lifelong learning opportunities that will inspire individuals, enhance futures, and enrich lives. YSU inspires individuals by cultivating a curiosity for life-long learning; enhances the futures of our students by empowering them to discover, disseminate and apply their knowledge; and enriches the region by fostering collaboration and the advancement of civic, scientific, and technological development. YSU’s culture of enrichment flourishes in our intellectually diverse, accessible, and quality education. Work Schedule: Typically, Monday through Friday. Teaching assignments may be remote or at various locations. Primary Location: Youngstown Qualifications and Competencies Required Certifications, Training, and/or Licensures: None. Sponsorship and/or Work Authorization Status: Must be currently authorized to work in the United States on a full-time basis. Minimum Qualifications: An earned doctorate in international education, higher education, educational leadership, or a related field, or a master's degree in education with a minimum of five years of experience managing or supporting international education programs. At least three years of relevant professional experience managing or supporting international education programs. Must be currently authorized to work in the United States on a full-time basis. Preferred Qualifications: Experience leading a study abroad office, managing an education abroad portfolio, or overseeing international health, safety, and risk management. Experience developing institutional travel policies, conducting program or partner reviews, training faculty and student travelers, and coordinating responses to international emergencies. Experience addressing student mental health, accessibility, and the needs of diverse participants in education abroad. Familiarity with professional standards and resources of the Forum on Education Abroad and NAFSA: Association of International Educators. Experience serving as a designated school official (DSO/PDSO) and responsible officer or alternate responsible officer (RO/ARO), developing immigration advising procedures, and training staff on F-1 and J-1 compliance. Successful graduate-level teaching experience, particularly in online or accelerated courses, and experience using a learning management system. Demonstrated success in the design and delivery of online graduate-level instruction. Physical Requirements: In accordance with the U.S. Department of Labor physical demands strength ratings, this position will perform sedentary work. Sedentary: work involves exerting up to 10 pounds of force occasionally or a negligible amount of force frequently to lift, carry, push, pull, or otherwise move objects, including the human body. Sedentary work involves sitting most of the time but may involve walking or standing for brief periods of time. Jobs may be defined as Sedentary when walking and standing are required only occasionally, and all other Sedentary criteria are met. Supplemental Information Please upload all transcripts as one PDF file. At time of hire, all candidates must provide official transcripts. Official transcripts must be provided in an unopened, sealed envelope and must bear the embossed or raised college seal, date and Registrar’s signature. This position is not eligible for benefits. 01 Do you have an earned doctorate in international education, higher education, educational leadership, or a related field, or a master's degree in education with a minimum of five years of experience managing or supporting international education programs? Yes No 02 Do you have at least three years of relevant professional experience managing or supporting international education programs? Yes No 03 What is the highest level of education that you have attained? Did not complete high school. High school diploma/GED or equivalent Some college Associate's degree Bachelor's degree Master's degree Doctoral degree Post doctoral degree Juris doctor degree 04 Please describe your related experience, including information describing how you meet the minimum qualifications for this position. Required Question Employer Youngstown State University (OH) Address 1 Tressel Way Youngstown, Ohio, 44555 Phone 330-941-1508 Website http://www.ysu.edu Apply"
    }
